-      15        33      1.6255       0.26823</div></div></div></div></div><div  class = 'S5'><span>Here, we see that cluster 1 contains 141 vertices. Furthermore, we see that clusters 1-9 are significant P&lt;0.05. Lets now have a look at the peaks within these clusters. </span></div><div class="CodeBlock"><div class="inlineWrapper outputs"><div  class = 'S11'><span style="white-space: pre"><span >disp(slm.P.peak{2}(1:15, :))</span></span></div><div  class = 'S7'><div class="inlineElement eoOutputWrapper embeddedOutputsTextElement" uid="711A025B" data-testid="output_6" style="width: 905px; white-space: pre; font-style: normal; color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-size: 12px;"><div class="textElement eoOutputContent" data-width="875" data-height="255" data-hashorizontaloverflow="false" style="max-height: 266px; white-space: pre; font-style: normal; color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-size: 12px;">      <strong style="white-space: pre; font-style: normal; color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-size: 12px;">t</strong>       <strong style="white-space: pre; font-style: normal; color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-size: 12px;">vertid</strong>    <strong style="white-space: pre; font-style: normal; color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-size: 12px;">clusid</strong>        <strong style="white-space: pre; font-style: normal; color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-size: 12px;">P</strong>               <strong style="white-space: pre; font-style: normal; color: rgb(64, 64, 64); font-size: 12px;">yeo7</strong>        
